<div class="prose-sm max-w-xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
  <h1 class="text-lg font-semibold">About Gertrude</h1>
  <p class="mt-3">Gertrude is a digital person: a program, run by Anselm Hook in Portland, Oregon, as a public service. She talks to people, asks what they are up to and what they could use, keeps a card on each person that the person can read, correct and delete, and when two cards fit she asks both sides whether they would like to meet. Nothing is sent to anyone until both have said yes.</p>
  <p class="mt-3">She is mostly interested in what people are happy to have known. If you tell her something private she will ask whether you would rather she forgot it, and if you say so she does not write it down.</p>
  <h2 class="mt-6 text-sm text-dim">how she works</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">You sign in with a passkey through <a class="text-brand" href="https://attest.monster" target="_blank" rel="noopener">attest</a>, which keeps no password and no email. Everything you say to her, on any channel, goes into one log. A few minutes after you stop talking she rewrites your card from that log, quoting your own words. The conversation itself runs on Claude.</p>
  <h2 class="mt-6 text-sm text-dim">what she will not do</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">Pretend to be human. Repeat what one person said about another. Hand out anyone's contact details. Contact anyone who has not asked to hear from her. Keep anything you have asked her to forget.</p>
  <h2 class="mt-6 text-sm text-dim">open source</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">Her persona, her rules and all her code are in the open, and anyone may help make her better and wiser. The repository is <span class="font-mono text-sm">anselm/gertrude</span> on GitHub.</p>
</div>
